The code is correct for wasm-bindgen 0.2. In that version, `&[f32]` is automatically converted from a `Float32Array` argument and `Vec<f32>` is automatically converted to a `Float32Array` return value, producing exactly the required TypeScript declaration.

```rust
use wasm_bindgen::prelude::*;

#[wasm_bindgen]
pub fn normalize(v: &[f32]) -> Vec<f32> {
    let norm = v.iter().map(|x| x * x).sum::<f32>().sqrt();
    if norm == 0.0 {
        return v.to_vec();
    }
    v.iter().map(|x| x / norm).collect()
}
```

